# Normalize line endings for every text file to LF in the repository,
# regardless of the checking-out platform's core.autocrlf setting. Without
# this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true (wl-dt26's setting) can
# silently rewrite the entire working tree to CRLF the next time something
# touches enough files (a branch switch, a fresh clone, a bridge-side
# edit) -- `git status` then reports hundreds of "modified" files that are
# pure line-ending churn, `git diff --stat` looks catastrophic, and
# `git diff -w --stat` (whitespace-insensitive) shows the truth: empty.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files: never subject to line-ending normalization or diffing.
*.xlsx binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
